English Is 1060nm Diode Laser Slimming Machine A Better Alternative For Stubborn Belly Fat, Love Handles And Other Body Fat?
Is 1060nm Diode Laser Slimming Machine A Better Alternative For Stubborn Belly Fat, Love Handles And Other Body Fat?
Rather than using cold, 1060nm diode laser slimming machine uses heat from lasers to kill fat cells. It has the same general process—fat cells are targeted, killed, and slowly excreted by the body.
1060nm diode laser slimming machine is ideal for people who have small areas of stubborn fat but otherwise are in good physical condition. The results are also permanent as long as the patient maintains their weight and physical health.
The shape of the device makes it hard to use on curved body parts, so it’s a little more limited than other options. Some patients report feeling a slight burning sensation due to the heat, although the device does have cooling on during the treatment.
1060nm diode laser slimming machine is more convenient
treating two areas in 25 minutes with 1060nm diode laser slimming machine is a big time saver over spending an hour per section with cryolipolysis. And since there’s no downtime with 1060nm diode laser slimming machine, you can receive a treatment and go right back to your busy life.
Most people with lighter skin should feel no pain as they will undergo hair removal with the 808nm Diode Laser Semi Permanent Hair Reduction. It is considered the latest and most pain free form of hair removal.
The Diode 808 Laser is the gold standard in Permanent Hair Removal and is suitable on all pigmented hair and skin types—including tanned skin. For darker skin types appropriate confluences (energy levels) are generally lower and appropriate pulse widths (duration of exposure) are generally longer addition with the cooling touch system to prevent damage to the epidermis.
Pay attention to sun protection one month before treatment; do not do epilation, hair removal cream or electrolytic hair removal for two weeks before treatment.
Two weeks before and after treatment, interventions such as fillers or other injections are prohibited.
