On February 4, Princess Arunrasmy’s cabinet office announced she decided to withdraw from the party, stating that she would no longer be involved or have any role in the party.
Shortly before his death, Prince Ranariddh discussed a merger between Funcinpec and the Khmer National United Party (KNUP), led by Nhek Bun Chhay, a former Funcinpec party senior officer. In September 2021 the two agreed to merge their parties before the 2022 commune election.
Cambodia will hold the commune election in June 2022 and the general election in 2023. Since the CNRP, the country’s main opposition party, was dissolved in 2017, observers say the competition will be little more than a game with no viable challengers to the CPP.
Analyst Meas Nee noted that many of Funcinpec’s top leaders, who represented critical human resources, were killed or destroyed in 1997, while subsequent scandals among leaders resulted in lost support and a weaker party.
