Reverse a feature one piece (IE, a group of commits), It's a real headache in the last situation, While that is easily done if the flag –No-ff has been used.
Finally, the changes made to the release branch need to be merged again to develop, so that the releases future also contain these bug fixes.
The release is now completed and marked for future reference.
The essence is that the work of team members (in develop branch) can continue, while another person is preparing a rapid correction of the flaw in production.
Then, correct the error and make the commit the correction in one or more commit separated.
This is quite similar to how the Release branches are finalized.
Although there is nothing really extraordinary in this branching model, the figure at the beginning of the Post can be very useful in our projects.
