This because, the “Greek yogurts” sold in Brazil are totally different from those outside. High levels of carbohydrates are found, added high amounts of sugars and other compounds and even excess starch, to improve its consistency.
And many people, not knowing this, end up thinking that they are having great benefits by consuming these “Greek yogurts”.
Thus, pocket and health are damaged and even spending a lot and thinking they are doing the right things, they do not achieve good results. Always pay attention to the nutritional tables of these “saboteur” products.
These yogurts have a nutritional value as good or even better than imported Greek yogurts. They have, when natural, about 4-6g of carbohydrates for every 12-16g of proteins, and this without the addition of protein compounds, among others.
