In search of health and body care, there is a demand for different types of diet to have a healthier diet aligned with a goal of weight loss, maintenance, hypertrophy, strength or performance.
With so many options, you end up getting a little lost on which diet to follow and making it difficult to choose the best one for your goals and lifestyle. A good diet must meet the nutritional needs of the individual bringing well-being, disposition, physical and mental health.
Remembering that all diets must have guidance and monitoring of a professional nutritionist.
What supplements can be included in the diet?
There are several types: diets that reduce carbohydrate (low carb), that reduce fat (low fat), hyperproteic diets, dukan diet, points diet and many others.
It has in its menu a great restriction of carbohydrates, compensating with the increase of the consumption of fats and proteins. Usually between 50g to 200g of carbohydrates per day are allowed, and when it is reduced even further and reaches between 20g to 50g it is called a ketogenic diet.
The menu consists of meat and fish, cereals and whole grains, vegetables, fruits, oilseeds, all within the daily allowance of carbohydrates.
This diet does not restrict any type of food, it only values natural foods, encouraging the consumption of healthier options. the mediterranean diet
It is a diet based on fresh and natural food with a high consumption of fruits and vegetables, fish, whole grains and olive oil. It is rich in fiber and unsaturated fats with little consumption of red meat.
To lose weight quickly and in a healthy way, it is necessary to align the diet with a physical activity routine, thus increasing caloric expenditure and accelerating metabolism. Exercising is also part of a healthy routine, with several benefits for physical and mental health, promoting well-being and quality of life.
It depends on the diet protocol you are following, some have the need to eat every 3 hours, others only eat when you are hungry, and there are also those who do intermittent fasting where they only eat during the feeding window of the day. day, the number of meals may vary according to the number of hours that one is fasting.
