Understand what lipids are and their function within the body - Bodybuilding Tips
Os lipids can be classified in different ways, such as their size (short, medium, long and very long chain lipids), their degree of saturation (saturated or unsaturated), their function, their degree of polarity or solubility (and the higher the lipid, the lower the degree of water solubility).
In the diet, lipids are found in different foods in different proportions. However, the most common sources of lipids are oil and fat, remembering that what differentiates them are the physical state at room temperature, since oils are liquid and fats are solid or partially solid.
A intake of lipids it is essential and more than necessary for us to have a balanced diet and for us to carry out biological processes properly. This is because these molecules have not only an energetic function, but several other functions such as:
- Raw material for the production of bile salts (cholesterol);
Today's recommendation is to consume 15% -30% of the total value of the diet. This is what corresponds to more or less 60g of lipids in the maximum quantities and 30g in the minimum quantities.
