After searching everywhere for it, Loki informs him that Prymr the king of the jotun (a race of very powerful ice giants) is the one who has stolen it.
Prymr makes it a condition that he will return the hammer to its rightful owner if Freya, Thor's mother, is given to him in marriage. As usual, the good woman flatly refuses and, after making a council of gods, they have a brilliant idea: disguise Thor as Freya to infiltrate the jotun kingdom.
Finally, Prymr decides that it is time to bless the bride and sends for the hammer.
As I am sure that now you have taken a special affection for the hammer and you are dying to see a few Mjolnir tattoo ideas, We have prepared some considerations that you can take into account so that your tattoo is unique.
The next thing is to think about whether you want the hammer to come out alone or accompanied. By this we not only mean that it appears with its rightful owner, Thor, but that it can have other equally cool and Nordic-style elements: other weapons, ravens, skulls, horned helmets, runes... A second element can make the hammer stand out more and make the design a bit larger.
Finally, color is also something very important to consider. A) Yes, If you opt for a more classic tattoo based on the traditional hammer, a black and white design will look great, with some good shading, whereas if you're basing it on the Marvel version a splash of color can work really well, especially if you're basing it on the comics and not the movies.
