Y indicates the sealing degree of moisture-proof and water-proof invasion of LED display screen.
Let’s talk about the significance of X and Y numbers respectively.
0: Not protected. No protection against contact and ingress of objects.
Dust Protected. Ingress of dust is not entirely prevented, but it must not enter in sufficient quantity to interfere with the satisfactory operation of the equipment; complete protection against contact.
Not protected.
Powerful water jets. Water projected in powerful jets (12.5mm nozzle) against the enclosure from any direction shall have no harmful effects.
We can see that the indoor and outdoor water-proof classification of LED displays is different.
Because there are more outdoor LED displays on rainy days or in need of waterproof than indoor LED displays.
The protection level of the display screen is IP54, IP is the marking letter; the number 5 is the first marking number, and the number 4 is the second marking number.
The waterproof level of outdoor LED full-color display screen is IP65.
5 is to prevent water from entering the screen when spraying.
